                                <connections>
                                    <action selector="logoutOfAccount:" destination="ky9-yU-pPM" eventType="touchUpInside" id="VHh-gr-lLG"/>
                                </connections>
                            </button>
                            <textView clipsSubviews="YES" multipleTouchEnabled="YES" contentMode="scaleToFill" fixedFrame="YES" editable="NO" textAlignment="natural" translatesAutoresizingMaskIntoConstraints="NO" id="PSj-eP-rEs">
                                <rect key="frame" x="24" y="82" width="353" height="537"/>
                                <autoresizingMask key="autoresizingMask" flexibleMaxX="YES" flexibleMaxY="YES"/>
                                <color key="backgroundColor" systemColor="systemBackgroundColor"/>
                                <mutableString key="text">Attribution: firebase sdk containing FirebaseCore, FirebaseAuth and FirebaseFirestore was used for the app. The Multicast delegate was provided by Michael Wybrow.  The assets called background is screenshotted from https://csjcarondelet.org/eco-challenge-find-balance-on-the-equinox/. The assets for cow, forest, logo and sign were created with Gemini AI where I would pass in images from my A1 documentation and ask the AI to colour it etc... With said assets I also feed some of them into the remove background website https://www.remove.bg. As for the pet assets such as cat and dog, I obtained it from https://kasayaa.itch.io/kasayas-animals by buying. I also used the Animals API from https://api-ninjas.com/api/animals to fulfill the webservice requirement for the assignment. In terms of persistent storage I used UserDefaults to keep track of the cooldown timers and to check user's state wether its their first time logging into the app or not. The app also has local notifications that is triggered when we set a due date for our tasks. Tutorial that I have watched to assist in creating my app is learning how to use tab bars from https://youtu.be/pM-DaWjL_Xk?si=3a5Alu6wpM8lppXW. I also learned more about setting up constraints from https://youtu.be/3s9C3EtPL4M?si=qDzLH8ZfxhCdXjGz. Within the assignment I would place "generated by chatgpt" or "generated by gemini ai" in comments above a function to show that it's made by AI</mutableString>
                                <color key="textColor" systemColor="labelColor"/>
                                <fontDescription key="fontDescription" name=".AppleSystemUIFont" family=".AppleSystemUIFont" pointSize="14"/>
                                <textInputTraits key="textInputTraits" autocapitalizationType="sentences"/>
                            </textView>
                        </subviews>
